    "counterexamples": [
      "RGB 0x696969 -> ODA 251; both candidate palette tables have exact RGB match at index 252.",
      "RGB 0x7F0000 -> ODA 16; both candidate palette tables choose 14 by unweighted squared RGB distance.",
      "RGB 0x000000 -> ODA 18; the tested LibreDWG palette has equal black entries at 18, 98 and 178, so tie policy matters."
    ]
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The probes have no XDATA; the prior EED counterexample receipt separately covers selected EED controls.",
    "Different palettes or distance functions could fit these results. These cases do not establish ODA internals or universal behavior, and do not demonstrate whether Autodesk uses any candidate formula.",
    "The name-versus-unnamed comparison does not resolve color-book validity because most RGBs do not match the fixed RAL name.",
    "The original physical DWG graph and EED must still be preserved exactly, and the originating DWG has no observed serialized DXF group-62 fallback."
  ],
  "conclusion": "Do not synthesize a DWG-source DBCOLOR group 62 from either tested palette-nearest formula; retain the fail-closed complete-output gate until producer-backed fallback and source graph semantics are independently established.",
